From 041c526b90640609ea227611f087855c6372af5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:52:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Sodick wire refuses a lean before the first rapid

A WireU / WireV stated before (or on) a section's first positioning move
was cleared by onRapid, so the Sodick wire post wrote G40 G00, T91, the
C word and G01 as if the wire stood upright. That lean is now refused by
name and the section is not threaded or cut; the next section posts as
before.

The 4-axis refusal (no G74 / G75, no U V) stays: the 1998 Mark 21
manual states U V as offsets from X Y on the part's bottom plane with
plane heights measured from the worktable, which neither the machine
file nor the stream states. docs/decisions/1497-sodick-four-axis.md
records what is and is not confirmed.

Fixes #1497

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
